  "description": "By default a walk neither records nor goes below a name whose path through its disk's mount is past the 4095 bytes of a mergerfs branch, while its folder's is not, and a scan reports it in branch_path_too_long. A copy moved there is not read as deleted: while such a name is on the disk, a copy found nowhere is uncertain, so its file is kept and its other copy stays, with nothing in the trash. With walk.long_paths = \"walk\" the walk goes below every name. The tree is deeper than PATH_MAX, as the runner can make one.",
